# KEUR-INT-001 — internal reference (tracker / wiki id) must not reach a public repo.
# @implements ADR-061
#
# A public repo should not carry the breadcrumbs of a private workspace: an
# internal ticket id, a wiki page coordinate, or a non-public contact domain
# pasted into a doc or commit. Harmless-looking, but it links a public project
# to private infrastructure — and it is the kind of thing you only notice AFTER
# the repo is public.
#
# This BLOCKS (not warns): once it is in a public git history it cannot be
# unpublished. Catch it at the pre-commit gate, where the fix is a one-line edit
# before the commit exists, not a history rewrite after the fact.
#
# Detection = pattern over text. Generalise the SHAPE, never a specific name:
#   - a tracker/wiki coordinate (SPACEKEY/<long numeric page id>)
#   - a tracker ticket id after a common tool name
#   - a non-public contact domain, supplied by YOU via a local override rule
#     (KEUR_RULES_DIRS), so this public rule never hardcodes any one domain.
# A legitimate mention of a *tool* ("we use a wiki") is fine — the rule fires on
# an ID shape, not a product name.
id: KEUR-INT-001
ilities: [confidentiality]
maturity: 2
title: Internal reference (tracker / wiki id) in a public repo
category: pii
severity: critical
engine: pattern
action: block
skip_comments: false
target:
  extensions: .md .txt .cpp .c .h .hpp .py .ts .tsx .js .jsx .go .java .rb .sh .yml .yaml .json .toml
  # The rules corpus holds detection patterns (not real data); eval/ holds
  # generated run data. Exclude both so the guard does not flag its own examples.
  exclude_paths: rules/ eval/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/ tests/fixtures/
patterns:
  - regex: \b(Confluence|CONF)\s+[A-Z]{2,10}/\d{8,}
    message: "Wiki space+page coordinate (e.g. 'SPACE/21744320552') — an internal wiki reference. Replace with a generic phrase ('an internal RFC') or a public link. Suppress with keur:ignore KEUR-INT-001 only if this is intentionally public."
  - regex: \b(ClickUp|FreshService|Jira)\s+[0-9a-z]{7,10}\b
    message: "Internal tracker ticket id. A public repo should not expose a private ticket taxonomy — refer to the work generically or link a public issue instead."
confidence: 0.9
fix: "Remove the internal reference: replace a tracker/wiki id with a generic phrase or a public link. To also block your own non-public contact domain, add a one-line pattern rule in a local KEUR_RULES_DIRS override (keeps your domain out of this public ruleset). If a mention is deliberately public and safe, add keur:ignore KEUR-INT-001 on that line with a reason."
